{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840977-alternatives-for-the-computer-skill","id":840977,"title":"Alternatives for the Computer skill?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-02T16:23:30-08:00","id":840977,"title":"Alternatives for the Computer skill?","content":"So if you were replacing this skill for a chronicle set sometime around the turn of the 19th century, what would you swap it with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:29:16-08:00","id":840985,"title":"","content":"Enigmas is what Dark Eras suggests. Requiem for Rome replaced Computers and Science with Warfare and Religion, so those are options as well, though a bit more antiquated. For 19th century I'd go with Enigmas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:30:56-08:00","id":840990,"title":"","content":"Codification, if you want something close. To Craft and understand secret messages.<br /> Mechanics, but I don't know if crafts already cover this.<br /> Warfare, from Requiem for Rome, you can use this for planning battles and strategies.<br /> Religion, The 19th century saw the rise of Biblical criticism, so this might be a good skill to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:33:07-08:00","id":840992,"title":"","content":"I'd say, 19th century = determinism, maybe with Logic, the ability to draw conclusions ala Sherlock Holmes ... with the risk to go wrong because things are not always that simple","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T16:35:04-08:00","id":840996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Horodrigo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840977-alternatives-for-the-computer-skill?p=840990#post840990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Codification, if you want something close. To Craft and understand secret messages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Enigmas does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JPS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840977-alternatives-for-the-computer-skill?p=840992#post840992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say, 19th century = determinism, maybe with Logic, the ability to draw conclusions ala Sherlock Holmes ... with the risk to go wrong because things are not always that simple</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Investigation does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T17:03:51-08:00","id":841009,"title":"","content":"Something I've toyed with for modern times:<br /> <br /> Technology. It steals a lot from current Crafts, by dividing it up into pre-industrial Crafts, and industrial Technology in terms of what they cover. Basically it's more of an engineering Skill, that deals with the complex current technologies of the day; building a factory loom to mass produce fabrics, instead of building a wooden loom for one person to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T17:29:49-08:00","id":841023,"title":"","content":"Seconding Enigmas. I was never a fan of the (c)WoD ability it inherited its name from, but if you read the description of the Skill in Dark Eras it's quite solid. I tend to lean towards renaming it something like Systems or Secrecy or something, but it navigates mazes, creates and cracks ciphers, and deciphers secret societies that, while not necessarily supernatural, are no less arcane for it. Kind of the shadow-side of the Politics Skill.<br /> <br /> I'd tend to distribute technologies between Crafts and Science. Poor Science doesn't tend to see a lot of use at my tables, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:11:08-08:00","id":841041,"title":"","content":"I would replace the skill of Computers with Abacus if the setting precedes the invention of the Adding Macine or Slide Ruler.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 03-02-2016, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:11:53-08:00","id":841042,"title":"","content":"My only problem with Enigmas is it seems like &quot;roll to solve the mystery,&quot; or else becomes so dedicated to cryptography as to be hyper-specialized.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T18:28:22-08:00","id":841048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840977-alternatives-for-the-computer-skill?p=841042#post841042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only problem with Enigmas is it seems like &quot;roll to solve the mystery,&quot; or else becomes so dedicated to cryptography as to be hyper-specialized.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Roll to solve the mystery&quot; is part of why I didn't like its precursor Ability by the same name, and don't care for using the name Enigmas. The key to using it is making sure cracking a code is not solving the mystery, but affords a glimpse at it. If you decode a message from William that says to meet at sundown at Callahan's, come armed, and avoid Northtown because there are spies on lookout there, well. That's given you a bunch of names and locations and a little bit of context. What it hasn't done is trivialize an adventure in one roll. The average coded message doesn't contain a full thesis on the conspiracy at hand.<br /> <br /> It's got a limited field of applicability, but a useful enough one; substitution ciphers and coded drops can make for valuable communication with allies, black budgets might be written in code to conceal operations or fraudulent finances, and secret societies are prevalent from Mystery Cults to the Ordo Dracul. It's not something <i>every</i> game is going to get a lot of mileage out of, but I could say the same of Larceny, or Animal Ken. Or, relevant as it is, Computer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-02-2016, 09:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T21:51:36-08:00","id":841123,"title":"","content":"Oops, I actually meant turn of the 20th century, but I guess that doesn't really change the answer.<br /> <br /> I'd have to read the Dark Eras writeup, but isn't solving puzzles a specialization of Investigation? My first instinct would be to say Enigma would be redundant... but then I realized there's a similar kind of overlap between Empathy and Subterfuge regarding detecting lies, so maybe that's the way to go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840977-alternatives-for-the-computer-skill?p=841041#post841041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would replace the skill of Computers with Abacus if the setting precedes the invention of the Adding Macine or Slide Ruler.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, this gave me a chuckle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T22:10:51-08:00","id":841132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840977-alternatives-for-the-computer-skill?p=841042#post841042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only problem with Enigmas is it seems like &quot;roll to solve the mystery,&quot; or else becomes so dedicated to cryptography as to be hyper-specialized.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Investigation is much more &quot;roll to solve the mystery&quot; than Enigmas is, and I wouldn't really call code cracking all that overspecialized. I see more uses for it in most games than Science, which despite being incredibly broad doesn't have a lot of use in most CofD games I've seen. YMMV","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T22:18:44-08:00","id":841136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blitzburger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/840977-alternatives-for-the-computer-skill?p=841123#post841123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have to read the Dark Eras writeup, but isn't solving puzzles a specialization of Investigation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said: good Skill writeup, bad Skill name. Enigmas in Dark Eras isn't a &quot;solve a puzzle&quot; skill. It's cryptography, obfuscation and ciphers. Creating and unraveling systems of secrecy. It's what a spy rolls to crack an encoded message used by the Roman military or the British secret police, what a shadow archaeologist rolls to recognize the hidden message embedded in a forgery of the Mona Lisa, and what an aspiring member of the Ordo Dracul uses to infer which flowery occult titles and secret handshakes are real signs of importance and which are actually ways to trick inconvenient pupils into marking themselves for death.<br /> <br /> Basically: not enigmas as in riddles, but as in what Enigma machines do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T08:22:20-08:00","id":841905,"title":"","content":"I've flirted with Analysis, which would be the ability to process large amounts of information. To crunch data on mysterious weather patterns, build profiles of adversaries from their correspondence or ledgers, that kind of thing. Not <i>entirely</i> happy with the idea, but it appeals to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T20:14:26-08:00","id":842374,"title":"","content":"I've been considering writing up mechanical considerations for a campaign set in the Golden Age of Piracy, and while I was doing research I saw another rules hack that replaced &quot;Computers&quot; with &quot;Navigation&quot;. I thought that was a good substitution, though it's only useful in campaigns involving a lot of travel, especially the seafaring kind. So if you're playing a nautical story, I'd go with that. Otherwise, the rest of the suggestions seem good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}